Package: msamodel
Type: Package
Title: Mutation-Stability-Activity Model of Protein Structural Evolution
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Julian", "Echave", email = "jechave@unsam.edu.ar",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mathilde", "Carpentier", role = "aut"))
Description: Implementation of the Mutation-Stability-Activity (MSA) model of
    protein structural evolution, in which mutations perturb the structure and
    become fixed or are lost depending on their effects on stability and activity,
    weighted by stability and activity selection strengths, respectively. Given a
    single structure and its active-site residues, predicts structural divergence
    profiles in two representations, per residue and per normal mode. The two
    selection strengths can be set to chosen values or estimated from observed
    profiles by maximum likelihood, with delta-method standard errors. Predicted
    profiles can be analysed in terms of nested models in which one or both
    selection constraints are dropped, and decomposed as a sum of mutation,
    stability, and activity contributions.
